For $
u>0$, let $J_
u$ denote the Bessel function of the first kind, let $j_{
u,n}$ be its $n$th positive zero, and define the normalized Turán expression by $\Phi_
u(x)= rac{J_
u(x)^2-J_{
u-1}(x)J_{
u+1}(x)}{J_
u(x)^2}$. For every $n\geq 1$, the branch of $\Phi_
u$ on $(j_{
u,n},j_{
u,n+1})$ has a local minimum at some $\alpha_{
u,n}\in(j_{
u,n},j_{
u,n+1})$. If $ eta_{
u,n}=\Phi_
u(\alpha_{
u,n})$ denotes the corresponding minimum value, then $ eta_{
u,n}< eta_{
u,n+1}$ for every $n\geq1$, the sequence $( eta_{
u,n})_{n\geq1}$ converges, and for every fixed $n$, $ eta_{
u,n}$ is strictly decreasing as a function of $
u$: if $0<
u_1<
u_2$, then $ eta_{
u_1,n}> eta_{
u_2,n}$.
